assert search([1,1,3,3,4,4,5,5,7,7,8]) == 8
assert search([1,2,2,3,3,4,4]) == 1
```

This function works by using two pointers to efficiently narrow down the search to the unique element. The key idea is to check the middle element and adjust the pointers based on whether the middle element is part of a pair or not. This approach ensures that the function runs in O(log n) time complexity.

